sequenceDiagram
    title HealthGuard System Sequence Diagram
    autonumber
    actor Resident
    participant Web as Web Application
    participant API as Backend API
    participant Engine as NLP and Rule Engine
    participant DB as Database
    actor MHO
    actor Admin

    opt Resident signs in
        Resident->>Web: Enter email and password
        Web->>API: POST /auth/login
        API->>DB: Find user and verify credentials
        DB-->>API: User record
        API-->>Web: User profile and httpOnly auth cookie
        Web-->>Resident: Show signed-in application
    end

    Resident->>Web: Start assessment and submit symptoms
    Web->>API: POST /assessment/analyze
    opt Request has an authenticated user
        API->>DB: Resolve user from auth cookie
        DB-->>API: User record
    end
    API->>DB: Load non-rejected database lexicon entries
    DB-->>API: Lexicon entries and canonical terms
    API->>Engine: Analyze text and selected symptoms
    Note over Engine: Match and normalize symptoms; apply negation handling and explicit clinical rules.
    Engine-->>API: Matches, risk level, reasons, and rule triggers

    alt Authenticated resident
        API->>DB: Save assessment and normalized symptom links
        Note over API,DB: Assessment and HealthAssessmentResult share the assessments table. Existing Symptom rows are reused or created.
        DB-->>API: Saved assessment ID
        opt Non-emergency guidance is available
            API->>DB: Save assessment-specific pre-medication guidance
            DB-->>API: Guidance saved
        end
        API-->>Web: Assessment result, recommendation, and record ID
        Web-->>Resident: Display result and guidance
    else Guest resident
        API-->>Web: Unsaved result (ID 0) and guidance
        Note over Web: Keep the pending assessment in browser session storage for an optional sign-in or registration.
        Web-->>Resident: Display result and guidance
    end

    opt Guest signs in or registers and verifies email to save the pending assessment
        Resident->>Web: Sign in or complete registration
        Web->>API: POST /auth/login or registration and email verification
        API->>DB: Authenticate or create verified user
        DB-->>API: User record
        API-->>Web: User profile and httpOnly auth cookie
        Web->>API: POST /assessment/save-guest with pending input
        API->>DB: Load non-rejected database lexicon entries
        DB-->>API: Lexicon entries and canonical terms
        API->>Engine: Re-run assessment for signed-in user
        Engine-->>API: Matches and classification
        API->>DB: Save assessment, symptom links, and available guidance
        DB-->>API: Saved assessment ID
        API-->>Web: Persisted assessment result
        Web->>Web: Clear pending guest assessment
        Web-->>Resident: Show saved assessment
    end

    opt Signed-in resident views personal history
        Resident->>Web: Open assessment history
        Web->>API: GET /assessment/history
        API->>DB: Retrieve this user's assessments and guidance
        DB-->>API: Assessment records
        API-->>Web: Personal history
        Web-->>Resident: Display history
    end

    opt MHO reviews community assessments
        MHO->>Web: Open MHO dashboard
        Web->>API: GET /assessment/dashboard/summary
        API->>DB: Aggregate community assessments and case activity
        DB-->>API: Dashboard summary and recent cases
        API-->>Web: Dashboard data
        Web-->>MHO: Display alerts, cases, and analytics
        opt MHO records a case update
            MHO->>Web: Mark handled or add RED-case activity
            Web->>API: PATCH /assessment/{id}/handled or POST /assessment/{id}/case-activity
            API->>DB: Save handled status or case activity
            DB-->>API: Updated case
            API-->>Web: Updated case summary
            Web-->>MHO: Refresh case details
        end
        opt MHO reviews a symptom lexicon entry
            MHO->>Web: Open lexicon review queue
            Web->>API: GET /assessment/mho/lexicon
            API->>DB: Retrieve symptom lexicon entries
            DB-->>API: Lexicon review queue
            API-->>Web: Lexicon entries
            Web-->>MHO: Display entries for review
            MHO->>Web: Approve or reject an entry
            Web->>API: PATCH /assessment/admin/lexicon/{id}/review or /reject
            API->>DB: Save review status and reviewer
            DB-->>API: Updated lexicon entry
            API-->>Web: Updated entry
            Web-->>MHO: Refresh review queue
        end
    end

    opt Admin manages users and lexicon
        Admin->>Web: Open admin tools
        Web->>API: GET /assessment/admin/summary and /assessment/admin/modules
        API->>DB: Retrieve user and lexicon data
        DB-->>API: Admin dashboard data
        API-->>Web: Summary and management data
        Web-->>Admin: Display users and lexicon tools
        opt Admin updates a user or lexicon entry
            Admin->>Web: Change user role/status or add a lexicon entry
            Web->>API: Admin update request
            API->>DB: Save authorized change
            DB-->>API: Change committed
            API-->>Web: Updated record
            Web-->>Admin: Show confirmation
        end
        opt Admin previews clinical rules
            Admin->>Web: Submit sample symptoms
            Web->>API: POST /assessment/admin/rule-preview
            API->>DB: Load non-rejected database lexicon entries
            DB-->>API: Lexicon entries
            API->>Engine: Run the current clinical rule engine
            Engine-->>API: Preview classification (not persisted)
            API-->>Web: Rule preview
            Web-->>Admin: Display preview
        end
    end

    Note over Engine,DB: LexiconRule rows are administrative/reference data; live triage uses the explicit rule engine and does not read them.
